  "body": "**Description:**\r\n\r\nPlease note, this is Matrix specification extend proposal.\r\nReferring to: https://spec.matrix.org/v1.5/client-server-api/#mtext\r\n\r\nNotification (eg. play a sound when a new message arrive) is desired but not always require for all messages in a room where automatic notifications is enabled.\r\n\r\nExample, certain types of bot messages do not require notifications. \r\n\r\nNotifications on messages where notifications are not applicable, makes those messages a nuisance.\r\n\r\nI propose a message-level notification control property, hypothetically named notification, where message sender controls the notifications.\r\n\r\nIf the notifications are enabled for a room, and:\r\n1. If notification is true for the message, then client should render the notification (eg. play a sound).\r\n2. If notification is false for the message, then client should not render a notification.\r\n\r\nIf the notifications are NOT enabled for a room:\r\n3. Regardless of notification is true or false for the message, client should not render a notification.\r\n",
